From: Alex Scotti <alexscotti@gmail.com>
Subject: vdin: the VPP loopback can capture 1080p frame packing

The VIU1 write-back loopback (vdin1, /dev/video71) picks its capture format
from the current vout's size, and knows only 4096/3840x2160, 1920x1080 and
1280x720. Under HDMI frame packing the vout is 1920x2205 (both eyes and the
45-line active space; vinfo reads 1080p24hz 1920x2205 on the AM9 Pro), so it
fell through to TVIN_SIG_FMT_NULL and STREAMON failed with "invalid fmt", on
every input: nothing could capture what a 3D Blu-ray actually sends.

Map 1920x2205 to TVIN_SIG_FMT_HDMI_1920X1080P_24HZ_FRAME_PACKING, whose table
entry is exactly that active size, so the packed frame - VD1, VD2 and the OSD,
blended - can be captured like any other output. Symphony uses it to check
where each eye lands when the picture is shifted vertically.
---
--- a/drivers/media/vin/tvin/vdin/vdin_v4l2_if.c
+++ b/drivers/media/vin/tvin/vdin/vdin_v4l2_if.c
@@ -2040,6 +2040,11 @@
 	else if (h >= 1920 - err_range && h <= 1920 + err_range &&
 			 v >= 1080 - err_range && v <= 1080 + err_range)
 		devp->parm.info.fmt = TVIN_SIG_FMT_HDMI_1920X1080P_60HZ;
+	/* 1080p frame packing: both eyes and the active space, 1920x2205 */
+	else if (h >= 1920 - err_range && h <= 1920 + err_range &&
+			 v >= 2205 - err_range && v <= 2205 + err_range)
+		devp->parm.info.fmt =
+			TVIN_SIG_FMT_HDMI_1920X1080P_24HZ_FRAME_PACKING;
 	else if (h >= 1280 - err_range && h <= 1280 + err_range &&
 			 v >= 720 - err_range && v <= 720 + err_range)
 		devp->parm.info.fmt = TVIN_SIG_FMT_HDMI_1280X720P_60HZ;
